[38;5;252m[1m## What the project turned out to be[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Much smaller than the task template assumes: one C file ([38;5;10mc_src/src/driver.c[0m, 40 lines) and one Rust file ([38;5;10mtranslation/src/lib.rs[0m).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- **Feature combinations: exactly one.** [38;5;10mtranslation/Cargo.toml[0m has no [38;5;10m[features][0m section and [38;5;10mc_src/CMakeLists.txt[0m has no options or conditional compilation (only [38;5;10m-fno-strict-aliasing[0m). So [38;5;10m--no-default-features[0m and the default build are the same single configuration. [38;5;10mverify.sh[0m still enumerates combinations generically from [38;5;10mCargo.toml[0m, so it will fan out automatically if features are ever added.[0m[0m
- **Public API: one function.** [38;5;10mdriver(float x)[0m copies the float's object representation into [38;5;10mchar[4][0m and passes it to the static helper [38;5;10mprint_hex[0m, which prints each byte as [38;5;10m%02x[0m then a newline. [38;5;10mprint_hex[0m has internal linkage, so it is not an export of either library and is only reachable through [38;5;10mdriver[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Test setup[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mtranslation/tests/common/mod.rs[0m dlopen's both [38;5;10mc_src/build/libdriver.so[0m and [38;5;10mtranslation/target/<profile>/libdriver.so[0m via [38;5;10mlibloading[0m and calls [38;5;10mdriver[0m only through its exported symbol on both sides, then compares the raw bytes written to fd 1. Two wrinkles were worth solving:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mcargo test[0m does not emit the cdylib for a [38;5;10mcrate-type = ["cdylib"][0m crate, so the harness builds it on demand (once per test process, matching profile and feature set).[0m[0m
- Capturing output requires redirecting fd 1, which is process-global. Captures are mutex-serialized, and [38;5;10mtranslation/.cargo/config.toml[0m sets [38;5;10mRUST_TEST_THREADS = "1"[0m; without it, libtest's own progress lines land inside a capture and surface as fake mismatches (I hit exactly that). The harness now asserts on that env var instead of reporting a misleading diff.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mtranslation/tests/driver_diff.rs[0m covers ~660k inputs: representative values, all single-bit patterns and complements, every byte value in every byte position, a strided walk across the full 2^32 bit space, exhaustive 16-bit half-word sweeps, 200k deterministic-random patterns, and repeated/interleaved calls. NaN, sNaN, ±0, subnormals, and infinities are included.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
To confirm the tests can actually fail, I temporarily changed [38;5;10mto_ne_bytes[0m to [38;5;10mto_be_bytes[0m in the Rust source: 8 of 9 tests failed with precise bit patterns, then I restored the original.[0m[0m
